  "experiment_id": "EXP-DGR-EXTERNAL-CUMULATIVE-DEPENDENT-PIPELINE-CONTEXT-CONDITIONED-WRITE-GATE-ATTRIBUTION-083",
  "program": "Yggdrasil RSI corrective tranche: retained-state applicability/write-gate attribution",
  "question": "After recency-weighted updating changed retained payloads and behavior without producing a clean rescue, does useful cumulative memory require a context-stability write gate that prevents context-specific historical states from entering retained memory?",
  "hypothesis": "Y082 showed that changing update weighting is insufficient: the recency-half rule changed both selected payloads and downstream behavior but produced zero clean rescues and no favorable mixed signal. Freeze one bounded write gate over the byte-identical Y080/Y082 class representation. UNGATED_CLASS_WRITE reproduces the uniform multi-context class accumulator control. CONTEXT_STABLE_WRITE_GATE permits a historical class group to be written only when every contributing historical context independently supports the same successor byte for that class. The gate is computed exclusively from transfer, third, and fourth historical evidence before fifth-context outcomes. Written payload aggregation, representative keys, target-key induction, class-Hamming retrieval, schedules, scoring, and 16/7/9 capacity remain unchanged. This tests whether the missing property is explicit historical applicability/invariance at write time rather than memory size, recency, or transition selection.",
  "exact_parent_sha": "e13e971d1120fe75f18bcd36b9f27ab08afc28cf",
  "qualification_branch": "research/external-hosted-yggdrasil-dependent-pipeline-context-conditioned-write-gate-attribution-r1",
