    "eliminated_hypothesis": "a fixed 0.5 recency-decayed online update over the existing class representation is sufficient to make retained state transfer useful",
    "strengthened_hypothesis": "the retained representation may need an explicit applicability/invariance condition determining which historical states are safe to write before later retrieval"
  },
  "cause_effect_trace": {
    "observed_failure": "Y082 changed both retained payload selection and one downstream behavior while producing zero clean rescues, zero mixed signal, and zero partner collateral failures.",
    "residual_cause_under_test": "CONTEXT_SPECIFIC_STATE_WRITTEN_WITHOUT_APPLICABILITY_INVARIANCE",
    "exact_bounded_delta": "change only whether a historical class group is admitted to retained memory; do not change class representation, payload aggregation, target keys, retrieval, schedules, scoring, capacity, or accepted state",
    "control_rule": "UNGATED_CLASS_WRITE is byte-identical Y080 uniform multi-context class accumulation over every eligible historical class group",
    "gated_rule": "CONTEXT_STABLE_WRITE_GATE groups the same 17 historical rows by the unchanged Y080 class key; within each contributing historical context, sum exposed best_count evidence by successor byte and choose the largest sum with lowest-byte exact tie-break; write the class group only if all contributing contexts choose the same successor byte",
    "gate_threshold": "no fitted or numeric threshold; categorical unanimity of per-context historical successor identity only",
    "written_payload_rule": "for a passing class group, payload total, best_count, consistency, utility, representative key, cell_index, and map_best are generated by the byte-identical Y080 uniform accumulator",
    "target_retrieval": "for each frozen fifth-context SOURCE_CONDITIONED and LOCAL_ONLY target key, choose nearest written class group by unchanged class-Hamming and lexical tie-break; if no group is writable, reject activation and retain the original fifth-context behavior",
    "nonredundancy": "Y080 tested uniform accumulation, Y081 transition retrieval, and Y082 recency weighting. None tested whether historically context-unstable state should be prevented from entering memory.",
    "retain_revert": "Y083 is shadow attribution only; support authorizes only a separately preregistered bounded write/applicability correction or prospective validation, not accepted-state mutation."
  },
